<title>UK: GOLF-ELS'S UNBEATEN MATCHPLAY RECORD.</title>
<headline>GOLF-ELS'S UNBEATEN MATCHPLAY RECORD.</headline>
<dateline>WENTWORTH, England 1996-10-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the</p>
<p>playing record of South Africa's Ernie Els at the World</p>
<p>Matchplay golf championship which he won for the third</p>
<p>successive year on Sunday:</p>
<p>1994</p>
<p>First round - bye</p>
<p>Second round - beat Seve Ballesteros (Spain) 2 and 1</p>
<p>Semifinal - beat Jose Maria Olazabal (Spain) 2 and 1</p>
<p>Final - beat Colin Montgomerie (Britain) 4 and 2</p>
<p>1995</p>
<p>First round - bye</p>
<p>Second round - beat Lee Janzen (U.S.) 4 and 3</p>
<p>Semifinal - Beat Bernhard Langer (Germany) by one hole</p>
<p>Final - beat Steve Elkington (Australia) 3 and 1</p>
<p>1996</p>
<p>First round - bye</p>
<p>Second round - beat Steve Stricker (U.S.) by one hole</p>
<p>Semifinal - beat Mark Brooks (U.S.) 10 and 8</p>
<p>Final - beat Vijay Singh (Fiji) 3 and 2</p>
</text>
